hey 42 here if you've ever moved to a  new town or city you'll know how  difficult it can be to make friends  traditional advice is to sign up to some  kind of group or Club where you can meet  like-minded people you could take a  pottery class join a wine Appreciation  Society or become a member of the local  Glee Club I for one have made lifelong  friends in the Illuminati if you're the  more adventurous type though you might  consider joining aspiring a secret click  of agents who live under false  identities and meeting clandestine  locations to exchange top secret  information and tips on the latest  disguises one man who took this route  was William siebold a German American  who in 1940 joined what would become the  biggest spy ring in U.S history  seabelt had recently returned to America  after a couple of years in his native  country of Germany but if you'd met him  in those days he would have introduced  himself as Harry Sawyer a diesel  engineer that Alias had been given to  him by the Gestapo he'd cornered sibal  during his visit to Germany and politely  encouraged him to begin spying on his  adopted Nation the United States as most  people did after a chat with a bunch of  high-ranking Nazis threatening to murder  their entire family siebold agreed over  the following few weeks he was trained  in his Newfound profession before being  shipped back to the states to begin  collecting Intelligence on behalf of the  Fiora what Hitler and his cronies didn't  know though was that seabold had no  intention of doing their bidding whilst  being trained in Germany he visited the  American Consulate in Cologne in secret  explaining his situation and offerings  become a double agent working with the  FBI  when siebelt returned to New York in  February 1940 the FBI helped him set up  a new life as Harry Sawyer including  office space where he'd carry out his  work as an engineer or at least that was  the cover Story the real purpose of the  premises was to act as a meeting place  for siebold and other German spies the  officers were rigged with hidden cameras  and microphones and it was seabold's job  to get his fellow spies talking with the  FBI watching and listening in sibo  didn't know it at the time but the  clandestine operation was about to bring  him face to face with one of the most  accomplished spies and all-around  interesting people in history his name  was Frederick or Fritz Juba Dukan  and he was pretty much the leading  German spy operating in the U.S at the  time spying on the Americans was one of  the final assignments in what was a  truly remarkable life  seriously this guy makes James Bond look  like a stamp collecting geography  teacher if you Google Fritz jubair Ducan  many of the images you will find are of  a man wearing different hats literally  but Fritz wore many metaphorical hats  too including South African boar con man  journalist movie publicist Big Game  Hunter German Soldier British army  officer fictitious Australian war hero  hippo salesman hunting adviser to  President Roosevelt and of course spy  yes that list did include hippo salesman  can you imagine the ads only one owner  runs well low mileage a real head turner  but a bit heavy on fuel and handling can  be a bugger in the course of his rich  and colorful life Duquesne went by many  names and aliases at one point he even  assumed the identity of a real-life  Russian Duke that's why he's referred to  as the Duke in FBI fails but other  military code names included Dunn and  the Black Panther he fought in multiple  wars being caught and imprisoned six  times and sentenced to death at least  once but he escaped every single time  duken was born in 1877 into a boar  family in South Africa the boss being a  nation of pioneers and farmers who left  the cape colony of South Africa where  European settlement began and migrated  to settle in the interior of the South  African Wilderness his family lived on a  farm in the middle of nowhere and Jung  Fritz became a hunter like his father  at the clearly not so tender age of 12.  duken killed Zulu tribesmen who'd  attacked his mother with the tribesman's  own spear having displayed such powerful  survival instincts Fritz was apparently  judged to be ready for school in England  which is where he went next like so much  of his later life details of what duken  did after school are sketchy but we do  know that he returned to his homeland at  the turn of the 20th century to fight  against the British in the second Boer  War one of his missions was to deliver a  shipment of gold to a port in what is  present-day Mozambique this Precious  Cargo was being sent to a group of  exiled boars including then president of  South Africa Paul Kruger an argument  broke out amongst the boars escorting  Duquesne shipment and soon blows were  being traded when the dust settled only  Duquesne two wounded boars and some low  local Porters were left alive rumor has  it that Fritz finished off the two  remaining boars ordered the porters to  torch the wagons and hid the gold in a  cave before riding off into the sunset  on an ox as you do  to this day the missing gold has never  been recovered so if you're looking for  a dramatic career change and happen to  own a metal detector maybe mozambique's  the place to go during the course of the  war Duquesne was captured three times by  the British and three times he escaped  when he and his men were treated to  Portuguese East Africa he was captured  by the Portuguese too and imprisoned  near Lisbon again he escaped before  finding his way to England where with a  false ID and presumably a ridiculous  accent he enlisted as an officer in the  British army by 1901 he was on his way  back to South Africa once there he  discovered that his family farm had been  raised to the ground in line with the  scorched Earth policy implemented by the  British leader Lord Kitchener Dukan  learned his mother had been put into a  concentration camp whilst his sister had  been raped and murdered by British  soldiers Fritz was unsurprisingly not  best pleased with this turn of events  and so he and 19 accomplices conspired  to exact their Revenge by assassinating  Lord Kitchener but before they had the  chance to carry out their plan they were  sold out by one of the conspirators  wives all 20 men were sentenced to death  by firing squad but Fritz literally  dodged a bullet when he offered to  reveal bore military codes in exchange  for a stay of execution his reward was a  life sentence in the ironically named  castle of Good Hope in Cape Town where  he attempted to escape using the  time-honored spoon-digging technique he  almost made it too but when his plan  failed he was sent to serve the rest of  his sentence in a jail in Bermuda Fritz  soon added that prison to his list of  Great Escapes when he scaled a barbed  wire fence swam almost two and a half  kilometers through shark-ridden seas and  avoided Patrol boats and searchlights on  his way to safety from there he traveled  to the USA where he would settle never  to return to South Africa in America  Ducane supported himself as a journalist  even writing several novels before being  recruited as an expert on African  Wildlife by a congressman trying to  address the national meat shortage by  passing the American hippo bill of 1911  which aims to introduce hippo meat as a  staple of the American diet the New York  Times tried to dress things up a bit by  calling hippo meat Lake cow bacon but in  the end the bill wasn't passed so  Americans never got a chance to find out  just how good or bad the lcblt  sandwiches might have been it was around  this time that Ducane became acquainted  with Theodore Roosevelt joining the  American president on a hunting Safari  in East Africa as his personal shooting  instructor in 1913 duken became a  naturalized American citizen so it  seemed he was a Yankee through and  through but as anyone who's spoken to a  pretty girl in Thailand will tell you  things aren't always what they seem when  war broke out in 1914 Fritz lived up to  his name and became a German spy working  in South America he sank 22 British  Merchant ships by planting bombs in  their cargo holds when British  intelligence caught on to him he fled to  Argentina and attempted to fake his own  death by publishing an article in a  local newspaper describing his murder at  the hands of Amazonian tribes people in  Bolivia  when the heat had died down he slipped  past British intelligence and returned  to New York in May 1916 using an assumed  identity showing a pair of balls as big  as melons Duquesne had insured cargo on  the very ships he'd blown up when they  sank as he obviously knew they would  seeing because he was the one who  planted the bombs he tried to claim on  the insurance but when the insurance  company finished an investigation into  the whole Affair Fritz was arrested on  fraud that was 1917 and Duquesne was  making money on the lecture circuit  pretending to be a decorated Australian  war hero called Captain stalkton he  claimed to have seen more war than  anyone around and to have survived being  bayonetted three times gassed for and  stuck with a hook once but not even  Crocodile Dundee could escape the  clutches of an insurance company and  eventually Fritz was napped for his  crimes to make things worse when he was  arrested the authorities found damning  evidence linking him to the cargo ship  bombings the British were Keen to  prosecute him and Duquesne was set to be  extradited to the UK to face serious  charges but showing an unbelievable  amount of patience resourcefulness and  some great acting Duquesne pulled off  yet another great escape he feigned  paralysis in his right leg for two years  convincing both his jailers and doctors  that he was truly lame as a result Fritz  was sent to the prison ward of Bellevue  Hospital and from there he escaped  dressed as a woman just a few days  before his scheduled extradition duken  went to ground in Mexico and later  Europe but returned to New York in 1926  with yet another identity and a new  career as a movie publicist he is good  at it too even doing some work for  Joseph Kennedy the father of JFK but  that success came at a price Ducane was  a notorious criminal wanted by the  police and the more well-known he became  through his work the greater the chances  of someone recognizing him it took six  years but eventually someone realized  who deken really was and alerted the FBI  he was arrested again but this time  released on a technicality in the  mid-1930s with another War looming frit  was approached by German intelligence  and got to building a spy ring that  would eventually number more than 30  operatives these agents were mostly made  up of low profile types who infiltrated  many different Industries including  Aviation engineering and shipping and  they provided invaluable information to  the German leadership by this time dukem  was extremely experienced and was known  to be very careful about being followed  and observed but even he didn't see the  Trap that had been laid for him by the  FBI and the man we met at the start of  the story William siebold AKA Harry  Sawyer when the men first met duken he  was cagey but just like the rest of the  Nazi spies in his Circle he eventually  revealed all kinds of Secrets and  sensitive information in seabold's  camera rigged office  the FBI meticulously filmed recorded and  investigated aspiring for two years  building up a rock-solid case and in  June 1941 the FBI arrested Duquesne and  32 German spies in the largest  ever-american Espionage case that led to  convictions  19 of the operatives pleaded guilty  immediately and 14 were convicted later  the group received over 300 years of  jail time between them with Fritz  earning 18 of his own there was no  Escape for dukeen this time and he  served 14 years of his term before being  released on grounds of ailing Health he  would deliver his final public talk  titled my life in and out of prison at  the adventurers Club in New York in 1954  before passing away two years later at  the age of 77 with a life so full of  goods Glory crime and intrigue who knows  what he would have chosen to include in  that speech but I like to think hippos  got a mention  thanks for watching
 

